WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.340
One student says she
does not believe in God.

2
00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.200
Her friend says that God does not exist.

3
00:00:06.250 --> 00:00:07.630
They nod at each other.

4
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:09.620
Surely they agree?

5
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:12.110
Unbelief comes in many kinds.

6
00:00:12.160 --> 00:00:15.090
Some people live as if God does not exist.

7
00:00:15.140 --> 00:00:18.550
Others reject God because of
the suffering in the world.

8
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:20.450
And in 1869, T.

9
00:00:20.500 --> 00:00:20.670
H.

10
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.890
Huxley coined a word for
yet another view: agnostic.

11
00:00:24.940 --> 00:00:28.760
So do those two sentences
really make the same claim?

12
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:33.970
In this mission, you'll map the kinds
of atheism and agnosticism on one grid.

13
00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:38.490
Then you'll test the labels on people
with very different views of God.

14
00:00:38.540 --> 00:00:43.230
Your mission: find out whether those two
sentences really make the same claim.
